@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`price` in `src/index.ts` computes `total = dailyPrice * days` and is shared by `quote` and `book`, so one
+change covers both. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- 10% off for rentals of 3 or more days, shown by both quote and booking.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Other tiers, customer-based discounts, extra fields in the response.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Apply the discount inside `price`, the single place computing totals, so quote and booking cannot diverge.
+- Compute with integers: `Math.round(full * 9 / 10)` on the full price in cents; halves round up (totals are
+  non-negative). Alternative of truncating was rejected as it systematically favors the school without being
+  asked for.
+- Constants `LONG_RENTAL_DAYS = 3` and a 90% factor named in code. TypeScript strict, Node stdlib only, no
+  runtime dependency.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Rounding rule is an assumption; cents may differ by 1 from another convention.
+- Existing tests expecting 3-day full prices must be updated.
