+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+The school wants to reward customers who stay longer: a rental of 3 days or more should cost 10% less than
+its full price.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Rentals of 3 or more days get 10% off the full price (daily price × days).
+- The reduced total is what `quote` returns and what `book` returns in the booking, so both always agree.
+- Rentals of 1 or 2 days are unchanged.
+- The discounted total is rounded to the nearest whole euro cent (halves round up), since money is an
+  integer number of cents. Assumption, recorded in the design.
+
+**In scope:** rental pricing in `quote` and `book` (rentals, customers renting boards and sails).
+**Out of scope:** lessons, discounts by customer type or season, other discount tiers, new response fields
+(e.g. showing the undiscounted price), cancellation/refunds.
+
+No runtime dependency is introduced.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `rentals`: the Quote requirement changes so the total includes the 10% discount for rentals of 3 days or more.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: the `price` function computing the total.
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: new tests for the discount boundary.
+- Existing 3-day expectations in tests (12000, 8000 stays 2 days) are affected: 3 days at 4000 becomes 10800.
